78c5b00a-2803-49d7-9661-28d7b8b0655c	decision	{"scope": "A-share daily quant strategy implementation architecture", "project": "quant-agent-team", "summary": "Finalized strategy_spec as the implementation-grade quant strategy object for quant-agent-team.", "next_step": "Start a new conversation to design the quant code implementation architecture around strategy_spec and the previously aligned data layers.", "key_decisions": ["Split strategy artifacts into strategy_brief for research intent and strategy_spec for implementation-grade specification.", "strategy_spec is the formal engineering input for coding, backtesting, and review.", "strategy_spec sections are basic_info, inputs, derived_features, filters, entry_formula, exit_formula, ranking_formula, positioning_spec, risk_spec, execution_timing, and review_spec.", "entry_formula and exit_formula use structured conditions with one-level nested condition groups only.", "Supported operators are >, >=, <, <=, =, !=, in, not_in, contains, not_contains, between, is_true, and is_false.", "positioning_spec uses position_sizing_method, max_positions, min_positions, holding_period_hint, rebalance_frequency, and ranking_key.", "position_sizing_method values are equal_weight, score_weight, and fixed_slots.", "risk_spec includes max_drawdown_limit, max_single_position_weight, exclude_st, exclude_suspended, exclude_limit_up, and exclude_limit_down.", "execution_timing defaults align with after-close signal generation and next-open reference, using only data available by market close.", "review_spec must carry required_metrics, review_focus, known_risks, and failure_modes for auditability."]}	chat://codex/quant-agent-team/2026-03-17	[-0.08088718,-0.07630553,-0.066469796,-0.009271954,-0.06550216,-0.07859347,0.02237814,0.03794954,0.07892513,-0.043703333,-0.07237252,0.03584261,0.049922768,4.9892762e-05,-0.07678849,-0.035477836,-0.064527124,0.01864097,-0.08122701,-0.013236125,0.05848722,0.07269711,0.01985127,-0.011465507,-0.0396322